{
  "id": "Beyond_Assume_Breach_How_AI_Native_Security_Will_Reshape_Enterprise_Defense_txt_9",
  "content": "We're defining microspheres as hyper-segmented areas of the business that each have their own risk profiles, with specific tooling deployed accordingly. Picture an e-commerce organization that has agentic AI coordinating bot identification on customer-facing touchpoints, but an entirely different just-in-time smart intrusion-detection and prevention (IDP) running in the cloud to ID any misconfigurations that touch customer data, in real time. Over on the corporate network, execs have five approval layers before transfers of more than $25,000 can be sent through; and emails have a swarm of autonomous agents making game-time decisions on how likely something’s a phish. Just in case, they rotate credentials once a week—not that employees are aware, because it's all seamless and hidden behind an elegant single sign-on (SSO) solution. And all of it is coordinated via a back-office real-time orchestration layer that is itself operating on a need-to-know basis, where no one specific function is overprivileged.",
  "category": "Article",
  "source": "Local Storage",
